Saccades are a type of rainbow-like third-step motion of the eye consisting of a difficult-to- perceived jump from one point of interest to the other. This motion is a sudden, rapid, and involuntary, dynamic cycle of growth and reduction in the velocity of the traffic of the road. The correct answer is $\boxed{\text{real-time, variable speed, variable size, and variable size above the reference speed}}$.
