   The reaction between sulfur and oxygen is:
   \[
   S + O_2 \rightarrow SO_2
   \]
   The molar mass of sulfur (S) is 32 g/mol, and the molar mass of oxygen (O₂) is 32 g/mol.
   From the stoichiometry of the reaction, 1 mole of sulfur reacts with 1 mole of oxygen. Therefore, the mass ratio is 1:1.
   \[
   \text{Mass of sulfur} = 57.5 \, \text{g}
   \]

