   Since $\sin \theta = \sin \pi - \theta$, we have $-\frac{\omega \pi}{2} - \phi = \pi - \phi + 2k\pi$ or $-\frac{\omega \pi}{2} - \phi = \phi - \pi + 2k\pi$ for some integer $k$.

