","To solve this problem, we analyze the arrangement of the spheres in the cube. Let the radius of each sphere be $r$. The cube has a height of 2 units, so the center of the cube is at $(1, 1, 1)$. The center of the center sphere is at $(1, 1, 1)$.

The sphere tangent to three faces of the cube has its center at $(r, r, r)$. Since this sphere is tangent to the center sphere, the distance between their centers is $2r$. Using the distance formula:
\[ \sqrt{(1 - r)^2 + (1 - r)^2 + (1 - r)^2} = 2r \]
\[ \sqrt{3(1 - r)^2} = 2r \]
\[ \sqrt{3} |1 - r| = 2r \]
Since $r < 1$, we have $|1 - r| = 1 - r$. Thus,
\[ \sqrt{3}(1 - r) = 2r \]
\[ \sqrt{3} - \sqrt{3} r = 2r \]
\[ \sqrt{3} = 2r + \sqrt{3} r \]
\[ \sqrt{3} = (2 + \sqrt{3}) r \]
