\[ \text{Distance} = \text{Speed} \times \text time} = 10 \text{ m/s} \times 25 \text{ s} = 250 \text{ m} \]
The distance covered by the train is the sum of the initial distance between the jogher and the back of the train (150 m) and the length of the train (L m).
\[ 250 = 150 + L \]
\[ L = 250 - 150 = 100 \text{ m} \]
The length of the train is 100 meters.

