2. Galaxy formation: dark matter is believed to have formed dark matter halos, which are regions of space with a higher-than-average density of dark matter. These halos provide the gravitational pull needed to merge gas and dark matter, leading to the formation of galaxies. The mass and distribution of dark matter in these halos influence the properties of the galaxies that form within them, including their formation rate, and the formation of the first black holes.

