\[
M = \begin{bmatrix} m_t & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & m_t & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & m_t \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} 0.0114 & 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0.0114 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 & 0.0114 \end{bmatrix} \, \text{kg}
\]

\[
K = \begin{bmatrix} k_t + 2K_c & -K_c & -K_c \\ -K_c & k_t + 2K_c & -K_c \\ -K_c & -K_c & k_t + 2K_c \end{bmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 430,000 + 2 \times 45,430 & -45,430 & -45,430 \\ -45,430 & 430,000 + 2 \times 45,430 & -45,430 \\ -45,430 & -45,430 & 430,000 + 2 \times 45,430 \end{bmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 520,860 & -45,430 & -45,430 \\ -45,430 & 520,860 & -45,430 \\ -45,430 & -45,430 & 520,860 \end{bmatrix} \, \text{N/m}
\]

The eigenvalues \( \lambda_i \) of the system are obtained by solving the eigenvalue problem:

\[
\det(K - \omega^2 M) = 0
\]

where \( \omega_i \) are the natural frequencies.

