   \[
   t' = \gamma (t - \beta x/c^2)
   \]
   The wave wave-law for light is:
   \[
   x = c t
   \]
   Substituting this into the time transformation:
   \[
   t' = \gamma (t - \beta c t/c^2) = \gamma (1 - \beta) t
   \]
   Thus, the time interval \(dt'\) observed by the moving observer is related to the time interval \(dt\) in the source's frame by:
   \[
   dt' = \gamma (1 - \beta) dt
   \]
