   |00⟩ → |00⟩
   
   |01⟩ → |01⟩
   
   |10⟩ → |-1⟩|0⟩
   
   |11⟩ → |-1⟩|1⟩

2. **Toffoli gate**: The Tooffli gate is a 3-qubit gate, which is a controlled-controlled-NOT gate. It has three input qubits and one register qubit. The quantum cost of the Toffoli gate is 3, meaning it requires 3 controlled-NOT (CNOT) gates. The gate is defined as:
   
   |000⟩ → |000⟩
   
   |001⟩ → |001⟩
   |010⟩ → |010⟩
   |011⟩ → |011⟩
   |100⟩ → |100⟩
   |101⟩ → |101⟩
   |110⟩ → |110⟩
   |111⟩ → |111⟩

Thus, the quantum costs of the EPR and Toffoli gates are 2 and 3, respectively.",relevance,"# Task Description
