- \( V_2 = 8 \text{ L} \)

Since the process is isothermal, the temperature \( T \) is constant. We can use the ideal gas law to find the temperature:

\[
PV = nRT
\]

\[
T = \frac{PV}{nR}
\]

Using \( P_1 = 2 \text{ atm} \), \( V_1 = 4 \text{ L} \), \( n = 2 \text{ moles} \), and \( R = 0.0821 \text{ L·atm/mol·K} \):

\[
