   - The energy released by 1 g of TNT is 4680 J.
   - Let \( m \) be the mass of TNT in grams. Then, \( 4680 \, \text{J/g} \times m = 188.77 \, \text{J} \).
   - Solving for \( m \):
     \[
     m = \frac{188.77}{4680} = 0.0403 \, \text{g}
     \]

