v_e = -\frac{(1 \text{ kg})(90.0 \text{ m/s})}{5.97 \times 10^{24} \text{ kg}}
\]
\[
v_e = -\frac{90.0}{5.97 \times 10^{24}} \text{ m/s}
\]
\[
v_e \approx -1.51 \times 10^{-23} \text{ m/s}
\]

The negative sign indicates that the Earth moves in the direction opposite to the cannonball. The magnitude of the earth's velocity is \(1.51 \times 10^{-23} \text{ m/s}\).

