- \( \lambda \) is the wavelength in the medium
- \( n_c \) is the refractive index of the core material
- \( n_f \) is the refractive index of the free (superwire) medium (e.g., air or \( n_f = 1 \))

The given condition is \( n_{\text{eff}} - n_f \sim 0.3 \). The effective index \( n_{\text{eff}} \) is the reflection of the effective index of the waveguide, which is between \( n_c \) and \( n_f \). Thus, \( n_{\text{eff}} \approx n_c \).

